   "The parts are the same as in step 1. The power source with micro-USB cable is not built, because the circuit images don't show it.",
   "The battery's JST PH plug goes into the board's JST connector. The catalogue has one BATT port for that connector, so the battery is joined at lipo1 '+' to mkr1 BATT, and the connector carries both battery leads.",
   "The pushbutton sits across the centre gap in columns 8 and 9. Side 1 (1.l, 1.r) is on the top half at 8t.e and 9t.e. Side 2 (2.l, 2.r) is on the bottom half at 8b.f and 9b.f. Hole names follow the catalogue's convention (top bank rows a-e, bottom bank rows f-j).",
   "The black wire runs from GND to column 8 on the top half, which is side 1 of the button. The yellow wire runs from D8 to column 8 on the bottom half, which is side 2. Pressing the button joins D8 to GND, and no external resistor is used. The sketch uses interrupt wake-up on pin 8.",
   "No power-rail connections are used."
  ]
